792560777836050207-bb1c46fc-b471-40e2-b04e-3e191225e6f4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Lane f041, 2026-10-19: plan refreshed. The code stories now clean every teaching surface themselves, so reverting the docs story no longer makes the scan red; the red run restores docs/user-guide.md from c0cf1022671 instead. A draft of the test ran on story cubistic-patrician-deer's tree (914beb80203): the hint/route half passes, and the scan found exactly one line, docs/user-guide.md:659, which names the older 'rebar bridge-status' alias; the plan rewords that line rather than hard-coding an exclusion. Not yet reviewed (depends on scabby-loverless-pipit; Bedrock capped until 17:00 PDT).","timestamp":1792428535384295001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Lane f041, 2026-10-20: plan review BLOCK at ca042ec0f49 (2 findings), both valid, both fixed in the plan. (1) The scan's blanket `(?<!from )` lookbehind, meant to skip `from rebar import`, also hid the prose \"Import tickets from rebar export NDJSON\" at src/rebar/_lib_reads.py:110. The same lookbehind in story cubistic-patrician-deer's rewrite and AC grep is why that docstring survived. The plan now exempts only key `import` preceded by `from `, pins that prose case in a pattern test, and fixes the docstring. (2) The replacement-is-live check looked only at the first word, so `rebar bridge status/fsck/check-access/setup` went unverified past `bridge`. It now also requires the sub-verb to be one of the nested parser's subcommand choices (bridge and store). Dry run in a throwaway worktree at ca042ec0f49: with all edits, 38 passed; with only the docstring reverted, the scan fails naming src/rebar/_lib_reads.py:[110].","timestamp":1792553410863201944},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Lane f041, 2026-10-21: claimed (plan review certified at ca042ec0f492). Implemented as 33877ecf776 on origin/main ca042ec0f49, covering the new held-out test, the help-overview assertion, the _lib_reads.py:110 docstring and the user-guide.md:659 line. Red-then-green, recorded in the commit message: green, 47 passed across test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout, test_help_overview_coverage and test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout; red with docs/user-guide.md restored from c0cf1022671, the scan fails naming lines 391, 403, 404, 524, 555, 572, 605, 607, 644 and 659; red with only the docstring reverted (earlier dry run), it fails naming src/rebar/_lib_reads.py:110. make verify with PYPANDOC_PANDOC set to pandoc 3.9 is running; push follows.","timestamp":1792555680819683471},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Lane f041, 2026-10-21: make verify on 33877ecf776 with PYPANDOC_PANDOC set to pandoc 3.9 exited 0 (19,827 passed, 87 skipped, 0 failed; 21:08-22:08 PDT on 2026-10-20). Pushed as Gerrit 3059 patch set 1, which got LLM-Review +1 with 1 advisory: the scan asserted only absence and would pass vacuously on an empty or mis-scoped enumeration. Verified had not voted yet, so I fixed it: the test now asserts that README.md, AGENTS.md, docs/user-guide.md and src/rebar/_lib_reads.py were scanned. The fix was checked to fail closed with the scan prefixes emptied, and to stay red on the c0cf1022671 user-guide. Amended (Change-Id kept) as patch set 2, 39619b808f6a. The 3 contract files pass (47 passed). The only change in patch set 2 is that one test function.","timestamp":1792560082306908764}],"created_at":1788806443045238480,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6515055c-320b-4f7a-97d1-dbe47215e24c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3e7a-d8ef-ce56-4eb7"},{"link_uuid":"4463136a-a0f2-4c77-9619-53530565e7a6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5f27-ec22-3d61-4b0a"},{"link_uuid":"bb1c46fc-b471-40e2-b04e-3e191225e6f4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cfe2-c17f-19c0-4302"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nNothing prevents a future doc or script from re-teaching a removed verb, and nothing asserts that the hint registry's replacements are themselves live commands. Cites are on origin/main ca042ec0f49 (2026-10-20). The two code stories now clean every teaching surface themselves, so this story's proof that the scan bites uses the pre-store-move tree, not a docs-story revert.\n\n## Approach\nNew `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout.py` modelled on `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py:66-93`, parametrized over `_help_route._REMOVED_SPELLINGS`: (a) for every key, `route_for(key) is None`; `main([key])` exits 2 and stderr carries `invalid choice`, the key, and the exact hint line; the hint's word after `rebar ` is a live top-level route; when that route's parser has nested subcommands (`bridge`, `store`), the next word is one of its subparser choices, and for `rebar store <sub>` also a member of `_registry.STORE_ROUTES`. (b) A `git ls-files` scan of `docs/ templates/ examples/ src/rebar/ scripts/ .github/ AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md README.md` for `rebar <key>`, exempting only the Python statement `from rebar import` (key `import` preceded by `from `), not every `from rebar <key>`; a pattern test pins that \"tickets from rebar export NDJSON\" matches, excluding the frozen-history prefixes `docs/adr/ docs/archive/ docs/experiments/ reports/` and a whole-file allowlist (`CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py`). The scan covers all of `src/rebar/`. On ca042ec0f49 it finds 2 lines: the `docs/user-guide.md:659` alias mention and the `rebar.import_tickets` docstring at `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py:110` (\"from rebar export NDJSON\"), which the store story's rewrite skipped through the same blanket `from ` lookbehind; `import_tickets` is not an MCP tool and the docstring is in no golden. (c) `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py:110` becomes \"from ``rebar store export`` NDJSON\", and `docs/user-guide.md:659` drops `rebar ` before the historical `bridge-status` spelling (the bridge-vocabulary guard already allows the bare name in that file), so the dict-driven scan needs no exclusion. Extend `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py` to assert no `help/<key>.txt` artifact survives for any key.\n\n## Scope\n`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout.py` (new), `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py`, one line each in `docs/user-guide.md` and `src/rebar/_lib_reads.py`. Out of scope: all other source and docs.\n\n## Testing\nRed-then-green: in a throwaway worktree at the change's tree, restore `docs/user-guide.md` from c0cf1022671 (which still teaches `rebar fsck`, `rebar doctor`, `rebar compact-all`); the scan must fail naming that file, then pass on the merged tree. Both runs are recorded in the commit message. `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The test is parametrized over `_REMOVED_SPELLINGS` with no hard-coded copy of its keys.\n- [ ] Every hint's replacement resolves to a live route, its nested sub-verb (for `bridge` and `store`) is one of that parser's subcommand choices, and `store` subs are `STORE_ROUTES` members.\n- [ ] The scan is proven red-then-green as above (the commit message records both runs).\n- [ ] No `help/<key>.txt` survives for any removed key.\n- [ ] The test runs in the `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` selection (`not integration and not external`) with no marker beyond `unit`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 with `PYPANDOC_PANDOC` set to pandoc 3.9.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout.py","reason":"new held-out guard"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","reason":"no removed-key help artifact survives"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"one historical bridge-status mention drops the rebar prefix"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_reads.py","reason":"import_tickets docstring names rebar store export"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","3e7a-d8ef-ce56-4eb7"],["parent","e045-84a5-e545-4f46"],["relates_to","5f27-ec22-3d61-4b0a"],["relates_to","cfe2-c17f-19c0-4302"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"e045-84a5-e545-4f46","parent_status_uuid":"bfd29299-6d6d-4cac-99fb-c1132d136c62","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"2183-fa68-d48f-42fe","ticket_type":"story","title":"Held-out test: removed CLI spellings never return to a teaching surface and every hint names a live command","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b29e4f12-11b6-40dc-8109-b3f39f277cd4","a18974a9-43a9-4b89-8b3d-1af538f9f96c","fe602856-323c-4746-8e31-c8e3d8cbc0d7","fd0cf374-6796-4982-9c09-9ce067ff1955","bd67f350-2c74-418f-9645-05d822bb0fe8","7ef1b83c-0a40-4da1-8752-0058af2def4b","a8e558ad-8fbb-4edb-b2cd-700e71802018","96fd67f3-9135-45f6-b891-9f2928366582","5a7fbec1-dafe-44ad-ace0-6a5200df18a6","bfd29299-6d6d-4cac-99fb-c1132d136c62","cdf9eb8c-c186-4e33-a595-bead91cf95c6","456fead7-4824-4b44-8075-9436d99e2d77","4463136a-a0f2-4c77-9619-53530565e7a6","d094470a-9fc2-4112-8fb4-94c6943464af","bb1c46fc-b471-40e2-b04e-3e191225e6f4"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT"